  "description": "Google HeAR (Health Acoustic Representations) is a health-acoustic embedding model from Google Health, exposed here as a research-only representation model rather than a diagnostic model or cough-type classifier. The official TensorFlow Hugging Face artifact google/hear was verified on 2026-07-06 as private=false, gated=auto, license metadata=other, pinned at commit 9b2eb2853c426676255cc6ac5804b7f1fe8e563f, and governed by Health AI Developer Foundations terms of use. The wrapper verifies saved_model.pb SHA256 7c1c40b08dadb605633c01338cee4f70eb234c922c8b8f52deaa8f3e83240dbd, fingerprint.pb SHA256 a96364468d67f10bec29a2788f364ae47fa28ed5282eda69805d01dbeec6d548, and variables/variables.data-00000-of-00001 SHA256 08b7a1a0f63d988173d5c5d3c6a038507d93560751a956a0fa3dfb47e75eac99 before loading the SavedModel. The metadata-visible PyTorch artifact google/hear-pytorch at commit f791cd42437c3e268c8ac84707e3508900f65f1a remained file-download approval-gated in this environment, so it is documented but not used. Forge did not find an official serving container with Forge-compatible readiness and embedding routes, so this row uses a Forge-owned TensorFlow/FastAPI wrapper that accepts WAV, FLAC, MP3, or OGG audio via data URI/base64 or guarded HTTPS audio_url, resamples to 16 kHz mono, windows audio into 2-second HeAR inputs, returns a bounded 512-dimensional embedding plus input duration/sample-rate metadata and model_time_ms, and rejects requests unless research_use_acknowledgement=true. The pushed image forge-local/google-hear-health-acoustic-embeddings:wrapper-gpufix-20260706t0425z compiled, decoded the synthetic WAV default into a 16 kHz one-segment HeAR batch, scanned with zero fixed HIGH/CRITICAL Trivy findings, and is digest-pinned in all active Forge regional registries. Runtime hydration uses the pod-local writable /tmp scratch volume because Forge enforces non-root custom model pods and the shared /mnt/data hostPath root is not guaranteed writable for this image. This active catalog row has persisted matrix support for H100, H200, and L40S only; B200, B300, and RTX6000 remain failed/unsupported pending TensorFlow Blackwell-compatible execution. Google HeAR embeddings are research-only and must not be used for medical advice, diagnosis, triage, treatment decisions, disease surveillance claims, or pandemic prediction without a separately validated and approved model.",
