  "version_description": "Active catalog manifest for Google HeAR as a research-only health-acoustic embedding model. The official TensorFlow Hugging Face repository google/hear is accessible in the task environment after accepting Health AI Developer Foundations terms and is pinned to commit 9b2eb2853c426676255cc6ac5804b7f1fe8e563f. The PyTorch repository google/hear-pytorch is metadata-visible but file download is approval-gated in this environment, so this onboarding path deliberately uses google/hear and does not switch accounts, use mirrors, or substitute forks. Forge-owned FastAPI wrapper source is under services/models/hcls/google_hear_health_acoustics and exposes /audio_embeddings, /v1/audio_embeddings, /run, /v1/inference/google-hear-health-acoustic-embeddings, and /v1/health/ready. Docker build forge-local/google-hear-health-acoustic-embeddings:wrapper-gpufix-20260706t0425z produced image ID sha256:469aa3c5f203c1a6622319eec953867558c3fe1248a4ea2c16381b0b046cef46, was pushed to all active Forge regional registries at digest sha256:87c15cc3b52e36d1ebb56de358cb84745284c046493f9fbb49a58c90d27aaf11, and Trivy found zero fixed HIGH/CRITICAL vulnerabilities. Full matrix probes persisted support for H100, H200, and L40S; B200, B300, and RTX6000 remain failed/unsupported. The model is promoted to the public catalog as experimental, research-only, and default-ineligible with Blackwell cells disabled until a follow-up runtime fix validates them.",
